# Scanning Console OIDC Secrets
# TEMPLATE — add these fields to the existing scanning-console-credentials secret.
#
# To enable OIDC, add the following keys to your SOPS-encrypted
# scanning-console-credentials secret (apps/scanning-console/secrets.sops.yaml):
#
#   oidc-issuer-url: "https://keycloak.knowledgeondemand.net/realms/cleanroom"
#   oidc-client-id: "scanning-console"
#   oidc-client-secret: "<from Keycloak admin console>"
#
# Steps:
#   1. Decrypt: sops -d secrets.sops.yaml > secrets.yaml
#   2. Add the three OIDC keys to stringData
#   3. Re-encrypt: sops -e secrets.yaml > secrets.sops.yaml
#   4. Remove plaintext: rm secrets.yaml
#
# When these keys are present and non-empty, the Scanning Console will show
# "Sign in with Keycloak SSO" on the login page.
# When absent (optional: true in deployment.yaml), local JWT auth is used.
